  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through seven innings until Lombard's single broke it open in the eighth.",
    "what_this_means": "That's what late-inning rallies look like when they arrive on time. The Yankees were chasing after the first. Down a run after Baltimore scored in the opening inning. But didn't crack anything until the second, when a two-run swing gave them their first lead. For five innings it held. The game stayed locked at 3-3 through seven, with the offense creating chances but converting only three of fourteen RISP situations. Then the eighth arrived. Lombard singled to break the tie. A two-run inning followed. The bullpen. Hill, Cruz, Headrick, Blackburn, and Bednar closing it out. Didn't give it back. This is a team that finds its moment late when the moment still exists. They had the game. They finished it.",
    "what_to_watch": "Baltimore tonight. Kyle Bradish takes the mound for the Orioles with a 3.65 ERA. Cole counters with a 1.49 mark over his last four starts.",
    "story_state": {
      "trend": "stabilizing",
      "driver": "balanced",
      "confidence": "medium",
